		- [ ] <mark style="background: #CACFD9A6;"><strong>🏆 Next.js SSG & Vercel Caching Strategies</strong></mark> 
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Centralized `generateStaticParams` Wrapper Function:</strong></mark> **As a** Next.js app router, **I want to** manage static page generation for all routes from a centralized utility function, **so that** changes to static generation logic can be handled in one place for consistency and maintainability.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Route-Specific Static Generation Configuration:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** assign each route an object describing its static page generation behavior, **so that** I can customize static generation for specific routes without duplicating logic.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Logging and Monitoring for Static Generation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** log and monitor which pages are being statically generated and how often, **so that** I can identify inefficiencies or bottlenecks in the static generation process.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 High-Importance Page Generation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** define a subset of high-importance pages for each route, **so that** only the most critical pages are generated at build time to reduce computational overhead.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Configurable High-Importance Criteria:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** dynamically determine high-importance pages based on configurable criteria (e.g., traffic, sales, or release date), **so that** I can adapt the definition of high-importance pages as the application evolves.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Analytics-Driven High-Importance Refinement:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** use analytics to track which pages are most frequently accessed, **so that** I can refine the high-importance criteria over time to better reflect user behavior.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Paginated Static Generation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** pre-generate only the first few pages of paginated routes, **so that** I can reduce build times while still serving the most relevant content.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Default Static Generation Strategy:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** define a default static generation strategy for all routes, **so that** I can ensure consistency and reduce the need for route-specific configurations.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR):</strong></mark> **As a** user, **I want to** receive a cached version of a page while the new version is regenerated in the background, **so that** I experience minimal delays when accessing less critical pages.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Route-Specific Revalidation Intervals:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** configure revalidation intervals for each route, **so that** I can optimize the frequency of regeneration based on the type of content.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Tag-Based Revalidation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** group related pages using tags or cache keys, **so that** I can revalidate multiple pages efficiently when related content is updated.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Webhook-Triggered Revalidation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** trigger revalidation for specific pages via webhooks when sensitive data (e.g., prices) is updated, **so that** users always see the most up-to-date information.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Purge CDN Cache on Webhook Trigger:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** purge the CDN cache for a page when a webhook is triggered, **so that** no user can access a stale version of the page after an update.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Serve Fresh Pages After Cache Purge:</strong></mark> **As a** user, **I want to** receive a fresh version of a page after a webhook-triggered cache purge, **so that** I never see stale data, even if the page has not yet been regenerated.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Fallback Rendering Option 1 (Stale While Revalidate):</strong></mark> **As a** user, **I want to** receive a cached stale version of a page if it is outside the caching window, **so that** I experience minimal delays while the new version is regenerated in the background.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Fallback Rendering Option 2 (Blocking):</strong></mark> **As a** user, **I want to** wait for a new version of a page to be generated if it is outside the caching window, **so that** I always receive the most up-to-date version of the page.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Secure Webhook Implementation:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** secure my webhook endpoints with authentication tokens, **so that** unauthorized users cannot trigger revalidation.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 Batched Revalidation Requests:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** batch multiple revalidation requests into a single operation, **so that** I can reduce redundant computations when multiple updates occur in quick succession.
			- [ ] <mark style="background: linear-gradient(to right, #00B7FF, #A890FE);"><strong>📝 OpenTelemetry Integration:</strong></mark> **As a** developer, **I want to** integrate OpenTelemetry with my application, **so that** I can monitor performance metrics like page load times and revalidation performance alongside error logging in Sentry.
